### Implemented by

- [Webpack as a plugin](https://webpack.js.org/plugins/module-concatenation-plugin/), [example](https://github.com/webpack/webpack/tree/master/examples/scope-hoisting) (they have really good docs about it)
- [Rollup](https://github.com/rollup/rollup)
- [Google Closure Compiler](https://github.com/google/closure-compiler) (we have a Parcel plugin to do this but it's pretty heavy and relies on the Java JNI)

### Pro

- Faster runtime startup
- Smaller bundles
- Easier to debug stacktraces
- Implements tree-shaking by design and probably in a better way using minifiers (side-effects)

### Cons

- A real pain to implement correctly given the current state of the ecosystem (es6/cjs, see Webpack bailouts)
- Makes parallelism more difficult

